course: dictionary
lesson: 10926
title: Words for giving your time
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A volunteer is someone who does a job without being paid, because they want to help. Read this: «Volunteers carry toads across the road in buckets on mild wet nights.» Nobody pays them, and they do it to help the toads. That tells you what volunteer means.
explain: Ask yourself: did someone make me do it? If the answer is no, you are volunteering. «Any volunteers?» asks a teacher, and when you put your hand up, you offer to do something nobody forced you to do.
explain: Volunteer can also be a verb, meaning to offer or to work without pay. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Giving is not only money; a volunteer helps without being paid, and time, help and kindness count too.» If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A volunteer is someone who works without being paid, because they want to help.
fact: To volunteer is to offer to do something, or to work without pay.
fact: To volunteer information means to tell it without being asked.
fact: Phrases to learn: volunteer for, volunteer to, any volunteers, volunteer work, charity volunteer.
fact: «Wikipedia», started in 2001, is written by volunteers and is free to read.
exercise: «Volunteers carry toads across the road in buckets on mild wet nights.» Why are they called volunteers? | They are forced to by the council | *They help because they want to, without pay | They are paid well for it | They live at the pond
exercise: Mia asks, «Any volunteers?» What is she asking? | Who is hungry | Who can pay for lunch | *Who will offer to help with the task | Who has been to the pond
exercise: Which phrase means offering to do a job without being forced? | fall over | pay for | run away from | *volunteer to
test: In «Giving is not only money; a volunteer helps without being paid», what does volunteer mean? | A kind of money | Someone who is paid a lot | A tired person | *Someone who helps without pay
test: To volunteer information means to... | write it in a book | *tell it without being asked | forget it quickly | hide it from everyone
exam: Which sentence uses volunteer as a verb? | Volunteers help at the beach | The shop needs a new volunteer | A volunteer is kind | *I will volunteer to wash the boards
